Original commit body from ec254900448835820d950c46463d375678acd124:

`emit_module_attribute_refs(scoped_path=True)` walks a scoped path
LEFT-RECURSIVELY and emits one `module_attr_ref` edge per nesting depth, because
the module/attribute split is syntactically ambiguous and the emitter cannot
consult the catalogue. `std::env::consts::OS` is module `std::env` with
attribute `consts::OS` OR module `std::env::consts` with attribute `OS`, so it
proposes every split and lets the catalogue pick.

That is right FOR MATCHING and a category error for COVERAGE ACCOUNTING. The
unmatched rows are not modules the analysis called into and could not classify,
they are alternative PARSES of one reference it DID classify. At most one
proposal per read can ever match, so every genuine N-deep scoped read was
guaranteed to contribute N-1 entries naming modules nothing ever called into.

MEASURED ON THE SHIPPED CLI, a zero-dependency crate whose only scoped read is
`let os = std::env::consts::OS;`:

  before: Verdict: inconclusive  rc 2
          "calls into 2 module(s) that the I/O catalog could not classify
           (std, std::env::consts)"
  after:  Verdict: confirmed_with_caveats  rc 3

`std::env` was correctly absent in both -- it matched. The other two were its
own collateral.

A PREFIX TEST, NOT A LINE KEY, and that is what keeps this from over-suppressing.
Two DISTINCT scoped reads can share a line -- `f(std::env::consts::OS,
std::fs::File::open)` -- and a rule keyed on `(src, line)` alone would let one
matching vouch for the other, silently removing a real uncatalogued module. The
proposals of ONE read are not merely co-located, they are NESTED, so the sibling
test is a component-wise prefix over MODULE slots: `std::envy` is not a prefix of
`std::env::consts`, and `std::fs` does not vouch for `std::env`.

THE MODULE SLOT, NOT THE NAME SLOT, and it was measured the wrong way round
first. On the analyzer's own edges the name slot carries the whole path
(`std::env::consts::OS`); by the time the coverage gate runs, WI-pubiv's
boundary-id remap has rewritten it to the BARE LEAF (`OS` / `consts` / `env`) --
exactly the shape where a prefix test finds nothing. Written against the name
slot, reproduced against a live survey, read as inert, corrected.

Scoped to `module_attr_ref`: a call edge carries one proposal per call, so
widening this would suppress genuine siblings for no gain.

